diff --git a/CHANGELOG.en.md b/CHANGELOG.en.md
index 37bb174..eb6e995 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.en.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.en.md
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@ Notable changes in Telsiz releases are listed in this file. Version numbers foll
 - Search by song name in Telsiz DJ: if the owner has turned it on, a command such as `/play lobby song` makes the server search YouTube for the song name and add the first playable result to the queue with its name, and the announcement goes out with the name right away. The search does not use the official YouTube API and goes against YouTube's Terms of Service, which is why it is off by default and the owner turns it on in Settings > General > Music bot through a confirmation dialog. The search text is not encrypted: it goes to the server and, from the server's IP address, to YouTube. The client's address does not go to YouTube, and the text is not logged. There are at most 10 searches per minute per person and 300 YouTube requests in the last 24 hours across the server, and results stay in a cache for 10 minutes. If YouTube changes its format or blocks the server's address, the search turns off for 1 hour after repeated failures and a warning is written to the log. While search is off or fails, a clear error message and a Search on YouTube link on the DJ card appear. Adding by link always works. The search has never been tried against the real YouTube, and the first live test has to be done on the server ([docs/DEPLOYMENT.md](docs/DEPLOYMENT.md#youtube-search-by-song-name)).
 - Automatic idle: if the mouse, keyboard, touch or a gamepad is not used on a device for 10 minutes, that device counts as idle, and once all of a person's open devices and tabs are idle, others see the person as Idle and the person's own status reads "Idle (automatic)". The first input brings them back to Online. A device in a voice room never counts as idle on that frequency, the desktop app also counts use of other apps on the computer, and the background windows of frequencies that are not open decide by the system idle time (a voice room in the main window does not affect this decision). Short taps on a gamepad count as input too. A chosen Idle, Do Not Disturb or Invisible status does not change. The information goes to the server's memory with the long-poll request (`idle` and the page id `tab`) and is not written to disk, and a session going idle is accepted at most once every 5 seconds. Since the tabs of the same browser share one session, the report of each page is kept apart, so a tab in use and a forgotten tab do not take turns changing the status. It can be turned off for this device in the Automatic Idle section of Settings > Privacy, where the time (5, 10, 15, 30 or 60 minutes) can be chosen. The server and members can see when a person went inactive.
 - Floating window (requests 7 and 16): while you're in a voice room or a direct message call, cameras, or profile photos and the green ring of the person speaking when there are no cameras, appear in a small always-on-top window (at most 4 cameras and 8 avatars, the rest as "+N people"). The window has Microphone, Back to App and Close buttons. In the desktop app it opens by itself when the window is minimized or hidden to the tray and closes when the window comes back, and on Windows and macOS it is excluded from screen sharing. In the browser it opens with the Floating Window button on the radio card (document picture-in-picture in Chrome, Edge and desktop Firefox 151 and later, a video window without buttons is tried elsewhere), and Chrome and Edge also open it by themselves when you switch tabs. Opening by itself can be turned off in Settings > Voice and Video. The person sharing their screen can close the preview with Minimize (sharing continues and Show Preview appears in the chip in the top bar), and the Floating Window button in the stream header shows the room and a Stop button to the person sharing and the watched stream to a viewer. In the desktop app this window is the only exception to the new window rule: it opens only with a single-use name from the main process, has no preload script and no permissions, and cannot navigate anywhere.
+- Content reports: someone else's message can be reported to the frequency owner and admins with Report Message in the message toolbar or the Message actions menu, and a person with Report User on their profile card. You choose a reason (Spam, Harassment, Illegal content or Other) and can write an optional note. The text of a message in a text room is attached automatically, the text of a direct message only if you tick the box. The note and the message text are encrypted with the group key, the server only sees who reported whom, which message and for what reason. The owner and admins see reports in Settings > Members > Reports, can jump to a message in a text room and close a report with Mark Resolved, and new reports appear on their own while the list is open. New API endpoints: `POST /api/reports`, `GET /api/reports` and `POST /api/reports/resolve`. At most 10 reports per user per hour are accepted and the server keeps at most 500 records.
 
 ### Changes
 
